[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3756006116","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114998#issuecomment-3756006116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114998","id":3756006116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7f4Brk","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T17:20:07Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:20:07Z","body":"I suspect this is related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111129 and the discussion in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112425#issuecomment-3493579597. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111129 was merged in dev2 so it lines up with your observation that the regression happened in dev2. \n\nThe difference is that in dev1, your game would stall for several seconds while loading due to compiling shader pipelines, that stall has been pushed into background threads, but the trade off is that Godot will now stall if you try to _free_ those shader pipelines while they are not finished compiling. \n\nQueue freeing a MeshInstance right after creating it will always be a waste of resources and is best avoided. I'm surprised it isn't leading to stalls in 4.5 in your main project. That being said, we should do what we can to reduce the impact of this change\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3756006116/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3756027287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114998#issuecomment-3756027287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114998","id":3756027287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7f4G2X","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T17:24:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:24:38Z","body":"(In the future please fill in the tested versions with what versions the bug occurs in and not, see the suggestion in the report template)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3756027287/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144364680","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114998#issuecomment-4144364680","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114998","id":4144364680,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73BfyI","user":{"login":"namedtoaster","id":13757806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzU3ODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13757806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster","html_url":"https://github.com/namedtoaster","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T18:09:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T18:09:13Z","body":"I took a look at this and wanted to throw out a thought. What if instead of immediately freeing the shader when its last user is gone, we just mark the frame and wait a few frames to let any background pipeline compilations finish. Then after ~5 frames, if there are still no users, free the shader. By that point clear_pipelines() shouldn't have anything to block on.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144364680/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144402008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114998#issuecomment-4144402008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114998","id":4144402008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73Bo5Y","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T18:15:37Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T18:15:37Z","body":"> I took a look at this and wanted to throw out a thought. What if instead of immediately freeing the shader when its last user is gone, we just mark the frame and wait a few frames to let any background pipeline compilations finish. Then after ~5 frames, if there are still no users, free the shader. By that point clear_pipelines() shouldn't have anything to block on.\n\nYa, that (or something like it) is the right approach. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116540 which moves us in that direction. Not sure if it fixes this specific issue, but it's the same general approach we should be taking","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144402008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144459978","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114998#issuecomment-4144459978","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114998","id":4144459978,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73B3DK","user":{"login":"namedtoaster","id":13757806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzU3ODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13757806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster","html_url":"https://github.com/namedtoaster","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namedtoaster/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T18:26:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T18:26:49Z","body":"> Ya, that (or something like it) is the right approach. See [#116540](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116540) which moves us in that direction. Not sure if it fixes this specific issue, but it's the same general approach we should be taking\n\nOk nice. Looks like it's moving all resource freeing to the background. I have some changes that would be more targeted to this issue, lmk and I can add a PR","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144459978/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4149685387","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114998#issuecomment-4149685387","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114998","id":4149685387,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73VyyL","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-29T08:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-03-29T08:19:18Z","body":"> > Ya, that (or something like it) is the right approach. See [#